1265
00:49:45.020 --> 00:49:45.820
I was right.

1266
00:49:46.540 --> 00:49:47.860
I was right.

1267
00:49:48.180 --> 00:49:48.860
What is it?

1268
00:49:48.860 --> 00:49:53.860
She said, we shot the restaurant on the New York street on the Universal back lot.

1269
00:49:54.060 --> 00:49:54.460
Oh.

1270
00:49:54.720 --> 00:49:56.040
I know the New York street.

1271
00:49:56.180 --> 00:49:56.500
Yes.

1272
00:49:56.620 --> 00:49:56.780
Yeah.

1273
00:49:57.000 --> 00:49:57.720
Now, here's the thing.

1274
00:49:57.820 --> 00:50:04.020
When you shoot in a fakie restaurant, you have to create all of the business outside of the windows.

1275
00:50:04.020 --> 00:50:06.380
And this fakie restaurant has windows on two sides.

1276
00:50:06.380 --> 00:50:15.440
So if you watch this scene, not only do you have to fill the restaurant with all the people inside, you have to make all the business happen outside.

1277
00:50:15.720 --> 00:50:19.120
So you have to watch this because it's really, really cool.

1278
00:50:19.400 --> 00:50:21.120
You see cars driving by.

1279
00:50:21.120 --> 00:50:22.420
You see pedestrians.

1280
00:50:22.840 --> 00:50:23.880
All this is happening.

1281
00:50:23.880 --> 00:50:25.420
I asked Kelly about it.

1282
00:50:25.620 --> 00:50:33.080
She said we had 24 background performers inside the restaurant and 40 people outside the restaurant.

1283
00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:40.580
20 people were drivers and 20 people were pedestrians who were like parking cars or walking by.

1284
00:50:40.580 --> 00:50:53.220
She said, Joe Moore, who was their second second AD, and Elizabeth Robbins, their DGA trainee, and nine production assistants, had to help with all of the traffic direction.

1285
00:50:53.360 --> 00:50:57.760
And she sent me the map that shows the loop that the cars made.

1286
00:50:57.860 --> 00:51:02.620
And it reminded me of the proposal scene that John and I did.

1287
00:51:02.760 --> 00:51:09.940
