1545
01:00:15.240 --> 01:00:20.660
And it may be hints to the fact that Oscar is still in touch with other people from Dunder

1546
01:00:20.660 --> 01:00:21.100
Mifflin.

1547
01:00:21.300 --> 01:00:21.620
Yes.

1548
01:00:21.880 --> 01:00:24.560
Well, the episode is going to end with a mare talking head.

1549
01:00:24.960 --> 01:00:27.840
She says, you know, it wasn't perfect, but it was his first issue.

1550
01:00:28.380 --> 01:00:32.520
And she framed it and she put it in the hallway next to the other antiques.

1551
01:00:32.680 --> 01:00:33.680
It's very, very sweet.

1552
01:00:33.960 --> 01:00:34.160
Yeah.

1553
01:00:34.500 --> 01:00:37.560
Well, you know, this episode was directed by Ken Quapis.

1554
01:00:37.740 --> 01:00:43.260
And we did reach out to him because I wanted to know, what was it like to return to the world

1555
01:00:43.260 --> 01:00:45.440
of mockumentary and did you have any challenges?

1556
01:00:45.900 --> 01:00:47.720
He wrote us back such a lovely email.

1557
01:00:47.900 --> 01:00:48.500
He did.

1558
01:00:48.860 --> 01:00:51.720
I remembered something that Greg told us when we visited.

1559
01:00:51.980 --> 01:00:57.240
He said, when we designed this space, we wanted it to look very different from Dunder Mifflin.

1560
01:00:57.380 --> 01:01:02.660
And they also researched what these old newspaper buildings looked like.

1561
01:01:02.800 --> 01:01:04.360
And they were big and expansive.

1562
01:01:04.680 --> 01:01:08.240
And beautiful old grand buildings with the big windows.

1563
01:01:08.680 --> 01:01:09.180
Yes.

1564
01:01:13.260 --> 01:01:15.920
So different from the Dunder Mifflin bullpen.

1565
01:01:16.080 --> 01:01:19.940
He said it was a challenge to visually connect people in the space.

1566
01:01:20.600 --> 01:01:25.580
He said he was very grateful that this opened with a conference room scene because he could

1567
01:01:25.580 --> 01:01:30.340
get everybody in the same room and really tell the story of who people were and connect them.

1568
01:01:30.500 --> 01:01:33.800
And he certainly has a lot of experience with conference room scenes.

1569
01:01:33.800 --> 01:01:40.400
But he also confirmed what Greg said, which was spy shots were difficult because when they

1570
01:01:40.400 --> 01:01:43.640
were designing the set, the set was designed by Susie Mancini, by the way.

1571
01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:47.240
And Greg said, I want you to use different blinds.

1572
01:01:47.260 --> 01:01:47.440
Yeah.

1573
01:01:47.660 --> 01:01:49.260
Because I don't want it to look like Dunder Mifflin.

1574
01:01:49.400 --> 01:01:51.960
So they chose these like tinier blinds.

1575
01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:56.000
But then when you open them, it's really hard to do spy shots through them.

1576
01:01:56.280 --> 01:01:56.460
Yeah.

1577
01:01:56.700 --> 01:01:59.840
The blinds being a bigger size was a good thing.

1578
01:01:59.840 --> 01:02:00.440
Yes.

1579
01:02:00.720 --> 01:02:04.600
But overall, Ken was just so happy to be back working with these people.

1580
01:02:04.780 --> 01:02:07.140
He said it's an amazing group of actors.

1581
01:02:07.420 --> 01:02:08.580
And he had a great time.

1582
01:02:08.800 --> 01:02:11.420
Well, I love that Ken is part of this world, too.

1583
01:02:11.560 --> 01:02:14.280
And I love seeing all the little crossover moments.

1584
01:02:14.580 --> 01:02:16.780
But I'm excited to get to know these characters.

1585
01:02:17.180 --> 01:02:18.240
Yeah, I agree.

1586
01:02:18.560 --> 01:02:19.600
Well, listen, everybody.

1587
01:02:19.800 --> 01:02:21.980
That's your breakdown of The Paper, Episode 2.

1588
01:02:21.980 --> 01:02:26.280
A big thank you to Kelly Cantley, Ken Kwapis, Chelsea Frye.

1589
01:02:26.340 --> 01:02:28.280
And Scott McGinnis, the Prop Master.

1590
01:02:28.280 --> 01:02:31.240
Thanks for answering our questions when we reached out.

1591
01:02:31.420 --> 01:02:33.200
And we'll see you guys all next week.

